# build output
/bin/
/dist/

# `go build ./...` in a module root drops one executable per main package into
# the working directory. Three of them were committed once and rode into the
# candidate bundle, which is how a candidate nearly received the reference
# connector compiled and ready to run. One line per command, so a new one is a
# deliberate addition rather than a silent inheritance.
/erp
/grade
/miniblp
/refconn
/seed

# runtime state produced by the two systems and the grader
#
# var/ is where make up puts everything the two services own: the twin's store,
# its inbox and outbox, and the ERP's export drop. It is regenerated by make up
# and make seed, so it is never committed - the shipped examples of the same
# artifacts live under examples/ and are captured deliberately.
/.run/
/data/
/var/
/grading/out/
*.log

# candidate bundles
/candidate-bundle/
/candidate-bundle.tar.gz

# editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
